  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Sueca. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Sueca (Portuguese: 'Swedish') is the most popular card game in Portugal and Brazil. It is a trick-taking game for 4 players in two partnerships. The game uses a 40-card deck and is notable for its Ace-Seven-King-Jack-Queen hierarchy (similar to Briscola or Tressette, but with 7 as 10 points). The goal is to take more than half the points (61+) in tricks. No talking is allowed.",
    objective: 'Win more than 60 of the 120 card points in tricks; first team to four games wins the rubber.',
    gameplay: "Player to dealer's right leads. Players must follow suit if able; may play any card if void. If any trump is played, highest trump wins the trick; otherwise highest card of the led suit wins. Winner of each trick leads to the next. No signals between partners.",
    keyRules: [
      'Must follow suit when possible.',
      'Trump suit from turned bottom card of deck.',
      'Highest trump wins trick; if no trumps, highest of led suit.',
      'No signals or communication between partners.',
      '120 points total in deck; need more than 60 to win a game.',
    ],
